Adds §9 to docs/investigations/TREX_TAIL_SATURATION_HABIT_2026_10.md,
the update of 2026-10-30: the work of 2026-10-29 23:47 UTC to
2026-10-30 16:32 UTC on the T. rex tail saturation habit, decisions
D-D56 to D-D58, from the run log's lines 760 to 801 and the folders
the earlier commits add. §9.1 lists it in date order, one ledger row
each; §9.2 gives the early-bias probe as verified (only the
policy-gradient term moves the tail mean; a push carried by tail_3's
own noise at s42's onset; the critic's bootstrapped value its source
from 2,097,152 on); §9.3 the early-warning curve and its follow-ups (no
loop-only rule separates the runs; the r9 held-out test fails; the
margins to the rail), with one correction: the early loop gains of r10
s42 that §4.7, §4.11 and §7 item 1 give (and §2 the first), -0.250 and
-0.386, came from a sweep that reaches the normaliser's clip, and are
-0.725 and -0.636 unclipped, the signs unchanged; §9.4 and §9.5 the two
critic-blind screens (line 1, not informative; line 2, reduced, p
1/70, with the checkers' wording); §9.6 what is answered and what stays
open; §9.7 the long critic-blind study, chosen and pending; §9.8
lessons 20 to 26; §9.9 the sources. The status block gains a dated
bullet, the date line and the ledger's row count follow, and §1-§8 are
otherwise unchanged, their figures as written.

Appends rows L168 to L187 to tail_record/ledger.csv, one per entry of
§9.1 and one for §9.8's lessons, as Python's csv module writes them
(every field quoted, LF line ends), after a check that the last row is
L167; the first 168 lines are unchanged (sha256 ff3acd39..., the
ledger's sum before). §9 cites no earlier row, and no earlier row
changes; the ids each section of §9 cites equal the new rows'
where_in_record (the record's own update_check/check_cites.py), but
for the status block, §9's opening and §9.9, which name the range, as
the status block and §8.5 do for the earlier rows. A new kind of
change, appended, defined in SOURCES.txt, marks the ledger's row;
tail_record/README.md gains the update's section and its ledger
bullet the new count.

The stance record gains §29 (§1-§28 unchanged, so §28.3's "why the loop
forms in training is open" stays as written) and a dated status note
at its top: a pointer to the note's §9, with the probes, both screens'
readings and D-D56 to D-D58 in short, and what changes in §13-§28 (no
certification; the question narrowed from mid-rise on; the long study
pending; the new folders and the two durable branches). NEXT_STEPS §3
gains a dated note (the next T-Rex session above is still a fresh
stance on physics r10). KNOWN_ISSUES gains Update 24 of the T-Rex
stance entry and a dated update to the action-saturation entry; the
docs index gains a note in the record's row and in the stance record's
row; the consolidation plan's D-D56 row links the note. CHANGELOG Added
gains an entry, and this change's status row names the note.
critic_blind_results/README.md now links the three folders added after
it (overnight_probes/, bias_screen/ and bias_screen2/), named in code
font until they exist.

SOURCES.txt gains the note defining appended, and the ledger's row its
new kind; SHA256SUMS still pins 2002 files, the ledger's sum changed
(sha256sum -c: all OK); the folder's README gains the entry, the note
under "What changed in the copies" and three re-check rows.

Records only: no library code, configuration, test, notebook, digest or
generated file changes.

