+"L170","2026-10-30 00:30-03:45 UTC","probe","Early-bias probe: one PPO update rebuilt at the r10 checkpoints; only the policy-gradient term moves the tail mean (first reading, unverified)","superseded","measured","EB, no optimizer step: at the local r10 F2 checkpoints (s42 and s80 at 1,048,576, 2,097,152 and 3,145,728, s42 also at 3,670,016; s60 at 5,242,880 to 8,388,608) one PPO update rebuilt (rollout, GAE, the full mirror-symmetric PPO loss); each loss term's first-order push on the deterministic tail_3 mean (plain and Adam-preconditioned) split by reward term, by state region (the rollout, the probe's bank, statue_settled) and by noise carrier, and set against the weights' realised change to the next checkpoint.","[measured, unverified; RUNLOG l770] Only the policy-gradient term moves tail_3's mean (entropy and value exactly 0, mirror-KL small). At 1.05M (s42 and s80) the expected update is null, yet the weights raised tail_3 about +0.15 over 1.05-2.10M in both s42 and s80. From 2.10M an upward pull carried by tail_3's own noise appears, driven by the critic's bootstrapped value (the GAE pull exceeds the critic-free MC pull; realised rewards push down; the critic's slope on the tail angle turns positive where the pull appears, 11/11 checkpoints); it grows 10x in s42 by 3.15M and is gone in s80. The r9 '-0.122' pull is reproduced in kind (-0.156 at s42 3.15M). [inferred there] The tail angle as an episode-phase proxy for the critic.","stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_bias/eb_summary.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_bias/eb_aggregate.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_bias/eb_realized.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_bias/eb_proxy.txt ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l11 (RUNLOG l770)","N03 (update of 2026-10-30; EB, RUNLOG l770)","§9.1; §9.2","RUNLOG l763 planned checkpoints every 262,144 steps; the probe read the local F2 checkpoints, 1,048,576 apart (eb_summary.txt), and missed s42's onset (1.204M), which the verifier reached by fetching the 1,310,720 pair (L171; MR §1)."
+"L171","2026-10-30 ~03:45-04:21 UTC","probe","Early-bias probe verified with corrections: a push on tail_3 carried by its own noise at s42's onset (1.31M); the critic-bootstrap source supported from 2.10M, unresolved at the onset","adopted","measured","VEB, an adversarial verifier with its own code (vb_update.py) and fresh rollout seeds (7001-7064, 7101-7124, 7201-7216), also on the 1,310,720 checkpoints of s42 and s80, which it fetched read-only from Drive; its critic-free test sets GAE against Monte Carlo returns on rows at least 200 from a cut.","[measured, VEB vb_aggregate.txt l27-l150; RUNLOG l771] At 1.31M (0.1M after s42's onset at 1.204M) s42 already has an upward policy-gradient pull on tail_3 carried by its own exploration noise: +0.00115 +- 0.00032 per epoch (t 3.6); r9-style bias pull -0.040 (-0.0398 +- 0.0071); the critic's slope on the tail angle positive (+0.0177 per degree). s80 has none then (+0.00011 +- 0.00025, t 0.4) and gets it about 0.8M later. The critic-bootstrap source is supported from 2.10M on (on-policy rows; GAE-MC +0.00372 +- 0.00099, t 3.7, at 2.10M; +0.02386 +- 0.00301, t 7.9, at 3.15M) but unresolved at the onset (+0.00048 +- 0.00045 at 1.31M) and not on the statue_settled state; mirror-KL, entropy and value terms play no part. The probe's own critic-error slope (the critic under-values a raised tail unless phase is controlled) was omitted; the episode-phase reading stays a hypothesis.","stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_early_bias/vb_aggregate.txt l2-l150 ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_early_bias/vb_realized.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_early_bias/vb_bank_weights.txt ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l12 (RUNLOG l771) ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/MORNING_REPORT.md l26-l40","N04 (update of 2026-10-30; VEB, RUNLOG l771)","§9.1; §9.2; §9.6","EB (L170): at 1.05M the expected update is null, and the noise-carried pull appears from 2.10M. VEB: at 1.31M s42 already has it, and whether the critic drives that first push is unresolved. VEB's used."
+"L172","2026-10-30 04:21-16:21 UTC","hypothesis","H-CRITIC: the critic's bootstrapped value drives the tail's climb (supported from s42's mid-rise state; the onset unresolved)","supported","inferred","The hypothesis the early-bias probe named (L170-L171): the critic values a raised tail, the policy gradient follows the advantage it bootstraps, and the observed-angle loop (L145) closes. Tested in training by blinding the critic to the tail_3 angle, from s42's 1,048,576 state (BS, L178-L180) and from its 2,097,152 state (BS2, L182-L185).","[inferred, from the measured L171, L179, L184-L185] Supported from mid-rise: from s42's 2.10M state, removing the critic's view of the tail_3 angle stopped the climb of the policy's tail command toward the rail (BS2 line 2, REDUCED, p 1/70); with the view, all four controls climbed and two reached the rail within 1.44M steps (BS2 REPORT.md). Not tested by BS (line 1, not informative: from 1.05M the control arm did not reliably rise). Not shown: other runs or states, a full run with the critic blinded from the start, the onset at about 1.2M, whether the critic would in time recover the angle from its other inputs, whether the habit moves to another joint (BS2 REPORT.md). Why the critic values a raised tail is open; the tail angle as a stand-in for episode phase is a hypothesis the verifier did not settle (MR §1).","stance_2026_10/bias_screen2/REPORT.md l60-l73 ; stance_2026_10/bias_screen2/score/score.txt l5-l24 ; stance_2026_10/bias_screen/score/score.txt l5-l9 ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/MORNING_REPORT.md l26-l40 ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l12, l35, l37 (RUNLOG l771, l794, l796)","N05 (update of 2026-10-30; from N04, N12, N17, N18)","§9.1; §9.5; §9.6",""
+"L173","2026-10-30 00:46-02:42 UTC","probe","Early-warning curve: the loop turns positive one checkpoint before the first tail over-bar episode in s42 and s60, but late s80 reaches the same loop state with none (verified with corrections)","n/a","measured","EW, no training, deterministic simulation and network evaluation only: at every saved checkpoint of r10 s42, s60 and s80 (37 in all) and of the 24 ECS continuations, the tail loop's gain G (d tail_3 command / d observed tail_3 angle on a 0-1 deg sweep, x 5.16 deg per command unit), its offset c0, the fixed point and the posture slope, on each policy's own settled states (seeds 5001-5010) and on fixed reference states, lined up against the ledgers' events; candidate report-only telemetry, never a gate. VEW: an adversarial verifier with its own code (reproduction, a held-out state set, the clip check).","[measured, EW NOTES l14-l72; verified with corrections, VEW vew_analyze.txt l1-l40; RUNLOG l768-l769] No loop readout meets the three conditions (present in s42 and s60 well before their first over-bar episode, absent in s80 and in the ECS s80 lineage) with any margin. G is strongly negative early (-0.73 s42, -1.38 s60, -1.38 s80 at 1,048,576) and climbs; it turns positive one checkpoint (1.05M resolution) before the first over-bar episode (s42 +0.35 at 3,145,728, FOB 3,670,016; s60 +0.31 at 7,340,032, FOB 8,126,464), but s80 crosses 0 at 8,388,608 (+0.07) and reaches the same loop state late (G +0.27, c0 +0.49, command 0.64 at 12M; PARK at 11.80M) with no tail over-bar episode. The best loop rule (G > 0.311) gives a one-checkpoint warning with margins 0.002 (s60) and 0.04 (s80), within training noise; no unseen positive test. The probe's bank tail_3 offset and the ledger's CMD_L (>= 0.3: leads 0.79M in s42, 1.70M in s60) are as early or earlier and already recorded.","stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_warning/NOTES.txt l14-l72, l188-l232 ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_warning/ew_analyze.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_warning/ew_series.csv ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_early_warning/vew_analyze.txt l1-l40 ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l6, l9-l10 (RUNLOG l765, l768-l769)","N06 (update of 2026-10-30; EW, VEW, RUNLOG l765, l768-l769)","§9.1; §9.3; §9.6",""
+"L174","2026-10-30 ~02:15-02:42 UTC","observation","Correction: the record's early loop gains for r10 s42 (VPOST) came from a sweep that reaches the normaliser's clip; unclipped they are more negative, the signs unchanged","adopted","measured","EW's section 5 and VEW's clip check: where the legacy 0-6 deg observation sweep (the verify_loop, posture_policy and VPOST definition) reaches the normaliser's clip (z >= 10 at 6 deg) at each checkpoint, and G on the unclipped 0-1 deg sweep.","[measured, EW NOTES l100-l123, l234-l245; VEW vew_clip.txt l1-l20] The record's §4.7 and §4.11 quote VPOST's G -0.250 (1.05M) and -0.386 (2.10M) for r10 s42 on the 0-6 deg sweep; at 1.05M that sweep is clipped beyond 3.74 deg, at 2.10M beyond 4.28 deg; on the unclipped 0-1 deg sweep these are -0.725 and -0.636. For s60 and s80 at 1.05M the corresponding values are -0.47 -> -1.38 and -0.48 -> -1.38. The signs hold. The 0-6 deg sweep reaches the clip at 89 of 181 unique pickles. VPOST's +0.261 at s42 3,145,728 is reproduced exactly on the legacy definition (+0.2607).","stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_warning/NOTES.txt l100-l123, l234-l245 ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_early_warning/vew_clip.txt l1-l20 ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l10 (RUNLOG l769)","N07 (update of 2026-10-30; EW section 5, VEW)","§9.1; §9.3; §9.6","VPOST (L164; §2, §4.11, §7 item 1): G -0.250 at 1,048,576 and -0.386 at 2,097,152 (0-6 deg sweep). EW and VEW: -0.725 and -0.636 on the unclipped 0-1 deg sweep, the 0-6 deg sweep clipped beyond 3.74 and 4.28 deg there. The unclipped values are used in §9; §1-§8 keep the earlier figures as written."
+"L175","2026-10-30 02:42-04:40 UTC","probe","The r9 held-out test of the warning signals: the probe bank's tail_3 offset fired in all 5 r9 runs by 2.06M, the cleanest negative included; the test fails (verified)","ruled out","measured","WR9, records only, its rules hashed before any r9 data was read (PREREG.txt, PREREG_STAGE2.txt and their .sha256 files): the warning signals the curve proposed, applied out of sample to the five r9 stance5 runs (s42, s52, s60, s70, s80; their ledgers and policy probes); VWF re-derived it with its own code.","[measured, WR9 wr9_r9.txt; verified, VWF vwf_r9.txt; RUNLOG l773] Only the probe bank's tail_3 signal was testable on r9 (the r9 ledgers have no CMD_L or saturated-actuator columns). It fired in all 5 r9 runs by 2.06M, including the cleanest negative, s70: the test fails. The verifier: evidence against it as a cross-run warning (its s80 'warning' a transient blip); the threshold translation (procedure X) was invalid. Its lead: a training tail-angle series exists in every probe (from obs_rms) and attributes r9's unnamed over-bar episodes.","stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/warning_r9/PREREG.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/warning_r9/PREREG_STAGE2.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/warning_r9/wr9_r9.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/warning_r9/wr9_procx.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_warning_followups/vwf_r9.txt ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/verify_warning_followups/vwf_procx.txt ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l14 (RUNLOG l773)","N08 (update of 2026-10-30; WR9, VWF, RUNLOG l773)","§9.1; §9.3; §9.6",""
