+"L186","2026-10-30 16:23 UTC","decision","Maintainer chooses the long critic-blind study to 12M, BS2's durable copy and this records change","adopted","decision","The maintainer's AskUserQuestion answers after the BS2 report: next step 'Long blind run to 12M (Recommended)': continue s42 from 2,097,152 to the full 12M, 4 runs (mostly critic_blind_tail3 plus a normal control), about 10 h on this machine after a ~2 h reviewed pre-registration (does the effect last, does the stance gate still pass, does the habit move to another joint); the durable copy, 'Push it (Recommended)' (an orphan never-merged branch, text only, no PR); the records PR, 'Yes, now (Recommended)' (docs-only, like #654). D-D58.","[measured, RUNLOG l798, l800-l801] BS2's durable copy pushed at 16:26 UTC (L185). The long study (LB): its build-and-criteria workflow (9 agents, no training) launched at 16:32 UTC: a harness builder (S 2,097,152 to the parent's end, about 12M; resume from the latest saved pair for a run of about 10 h), a measurement builder (the round's pinned tools: TAIL CLASS, ANY ALARM per actuator, GATE CLASS via the six-heading certificate, POSITIVE; validated against the round's classes for s42, s60 and s80) and a designer (criteria v1: Q1 stays off the rail, Q2 gate, Q3 habit moves, Q4 control rails; default 3 blind + 1 control, new seeds); then an independent build check, a scorer adapter, two reviewers, a fixer and a re-review of the fixed version. Pin and launch wait for the maintainer's confirmation; its result is pending.","stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l39, l41-l42 (RUNLOG l798, l800-l801)","N19 (update of 2026-10-30; RUNLOG l798-l801)","§9.1; §9.6; §9.7",""
+"L187","2026-10-30","lesson","Lessons of the night and the two screens: a control that can show the effect, a start where the effect runs, the fixed criteria re-reviewed, every write inside its own folder","adopted","inferred","What this record draws from L168-L186 (§9.8).","[inferred, from the measured L171, L174, L179-L180, L184-L185] (20) A screen needs a control arm that reliably shows the effect: from 1.05M the rise came by chance under fresh seeds, BS's gate (0.10) was not met and it could say nothing; from the mid-rise start (2.10M), where the probe verified the critic's push, the controls rose (median +0.46382 against a 0.20 gate) and the test read. (21) A pre-registered informativeness gate kept an uninformative screen from being read as a null. (22) With 4 per arm the smallest p is 1/70; a reading at that bound needs the spread caveat (S-3) beside it. (23) Re-review the fixed criteria, not only the first draft (BS's P2; done for BS2). (24) A sweep can clip on the normaliser: give a loop gain with its sweep range (L174). (25) An agent run as root can damage what every process shares (the /dev/null incident at about 01:05 UTC, repaired at 01:06 UTC; the probes' outputs unaffected); each agent writes only inside its own folder. (26) A durable text copy of each screen after its reading, never merged, keeps what the repository cannot hold.","stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/MORNING_REPORT.md l7-l24, l107-l111, l113-l136 ; stance_2026_10/bias_screen2/REPORT.md l37-l73 ; stance_2026_10/overnight_probes/early_warning/NOTES.txt l234-l245, l269-l285 ; stance_2026_10/critic_blind_results/run_log.txt l9, l21, l37 (RUNLOG l768, l780, l796)","N20 (update of 2026-10-30)","§9.8",""
